WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.511
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 15. Topic: Probability (Combinations, Inclusion-Exclusion). This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:12.931 --> 00:00:18.427
A bag contains 3 red balls, 3 white balls and 5 black balls.

3
00:00:18.587 --> 00:00:26.655
If 4 balls are randomly drawn from the bag at the same time, find (a) the probability that exactly 2 red balls are drawn.

4
00:00:26.815 --> 00:00:32.737
(b) the probability that exactly 2 red balls or exactly 2 white balls are drawn.

5
00:00:33.157 --> 00:00:37.707
STEP 1 — total outcomes.

6
00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:53.385
Key rule: Combinations. to the power n C sub r equals n! over r! (n-r)!. Drawing 4 balls from 11 gives to the power 11 C sub 4 equals 330 equally likely draws.

7
00:00:53.545 --> 00:01:03.638
There are 3 plus 3 plus 5 equals 11 balls. The number of ways to draw 4 balls: to the power 11 C sub 4 equals 330.

8
00:01:04.058 --> 00:01:08.974
Step 2. PART (a) — exactly 2 red.

9
00:01:09.134 --> 00:01:23.437
Key rule: Multiplication Principle. n(A times B) equals n(A) n(B). Choosing 2 of the 3 red balls and 2 of the other 8 gives 3 times 28 equals 84 draws.

10
00:01:23.597 --> 00:01:29.153
Choose 2 of the 3 red, and the other 2 from the remaining 8 (white or black).

11
00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:41.532
cubed C sub 2 to the power 8 C sub 2 equals 3 times 28 equals 84 P(exactly 2 red) equals 84 over 330 equals 14 over 55.

12
00:01:41.952 --> 00:01:47.375
Step 3. PART (b) — use inclusion–exclusion.

13
00:01:47.535 --> 00:01:57.380
Key rule: Inclusion-Exclusion Principle. n(A union B) equals n(A) plus n(B)-n(A intersection B).

14
00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:05.632
Both events count the 9 draws with 2 red and 2 white, so 84 plus 84 minus 9 equals 159.

15
00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:19.446
Let A equals exactly 2 red, B equals exactly 2 white. By symmetry n(B) equals cubed C sub 2 to the power 8 C sub 2 equals 84. A intersection B.

16
00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:23.240
2 red, 2 white and 0 black.

17
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:41.538
cubed C sub 2 cubed C sub 2 to the power 5 C sub 0 equals 9 n(A union B) equals 84 plus 84 minus 9 equals 159 P(A union B) equals 159 over 330 equals 53 over 110.

18
00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:50.155
So the answer is: (a) P equals 14 over 55 (b) P equals 53 over 110.

19
00:02:50.575 --> 00:02:59.643
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 15. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
